  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Plain summary"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The project moved from ad hoc printer setup and file fixes into a versioned, reviewable firmware and workflow package. The live printer stayed stock while the candidate was prepared and tested locally."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Printer setup and early print findings"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "OrcaSlicer was set up with stock T300 profiles, then refined for safer macro-owned startup behavior."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A Benchy printed successfully before first-layer testing."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "First-layer tests showed uniform gaps between lines, strong bed adhesion, and likely bed/mesh/flow interactions rather than a single obvious Z-only problem."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A missing-sheet homing accident made plate-presence defense a hard requirement."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The nozzle appeared visually undamaged, while the bed had a small puncture."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Community macro and runtime work"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "GerGo gantry-leveling was kept as the selected private workflow and protected from public redistribution."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "KAMP research led to using Smart Park and Line Purge concepts, with adaptive meshing held back because the stock bed range remained too large."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Factory corner purge and unsafe slicer startup were replaced in design by firmware-owned lifecycle macros."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "End and cancel parking were redesigned to lift first and avoid lowering the head."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Timelapse support was bounded so camera/storage failure cannot affect print safety."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mainline migration package"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pinned stack.lock.json records sources, versions, commits, hashes, and licenses."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Recovery and imaging tooling was added for eMMC capture, verification, write guards, and transfer safety."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Production and maintenance config trees were separated."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Safety policy, G-code admission scanning, Klipper extra, lifecycle macros, host service units, and UI defaults were added."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Full documentation, handover, audits, and release gates were added."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "GitHub publication"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The full public printer project was committed as 0590c50 Add T300 mainline migration candidate and pushed to GitHub origin/main after rebasing on the upstream t300-link documentation change."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Firmware and Orca refinement candidate"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Added admitted-print-only pressure advance from 0 through 0.20, with strict parameter validation and cleanup resets. A paused admitted print can issue only the zero reset so cancellation still completes. Adaptive pressure advance and uploaded TUNING_TOWER remain disabled."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Removed the generic 5 mm stationary extrusion allowance and replaced it with consumed retraction credit plus tiny, audited Orca numeric-rounding tolerances."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Added the read-only Printer Status action to Mainsail and KlipperScreen. Exact Klipper compatibility required its internal command name to be T_STATUS."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Added portable Orca 2.4.2 machine, filament, and process profiles, including zero-hop default and separate 0.4 mm collision-clearance variants."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Staged editable first-layer, orange bracket, and two Frieren review projects. No final G-code was delivered, and every necessary placeholder filament value remains visibly calibration-required rather than accepted."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Validated the candidate with 338 repository tests, 29 exact Klipper v0.13 production cases, one exact private-maintenance configuration load, 11 vendor Klipper v0.12 cases, exact Orca 2.4.2 normal slices, calibration-command contract tests, and a stage-bound large-format digital print."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Transcribed and researched the hull/floor-line tutorial against OrcaSlicer pull request 8107, Prusa's Benchy investigation, and Orca's setting documentation. Added a warn-first model review rule, flagged the camera bracket's base transition and inherited 25 percent overlap for owner review, and left both bracket and Frieren settings unchanged."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Recovery preflight and v14 candidate"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Read-only live inspection confirmed the stock eMMC/USB layout and old eMMC-first U-Boot behavior. The selected recovery route is now an owner-operated 1,500,000-baud serial console and the ordinary U-Boot USB command; kexec is not the primary plan."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Added locked recovery boot hashes, an offline media auditor, a no-automation serial helper, exact Armbian identity correction, and matching laptop/recovery-agent eMMC identity checks."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Built owner-local commissioning stage v14 with the exact purchased GerGo package confined to maintenance mode. Its one reviewed Z-stepper release command is allowed only in that private attended configuration; production G-code still forbids motor-release commands."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The final offline validation report passed all eleven checks, including the exact v14 stage, both Klipper versions, UI/services, secret scan, and a near-full-build-volume synthetic print."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
